r-run snapshots\n\n1. Send a message in the chat.\n2. `UPDATE configs SET config = '{\"compaction\": {\"tokenThreshold\": 9999}}', version = version + 1 WHERE scope_type = 'user' AND scope_id = '<userId>';`\n3. Send a second message.\n\n```sql\nSELECT created_at, config_snapshot FROM runs ORDER BY created_at;\n```\n\nRun 1's snapshot still says 1200, run 2's says 9999 — a config change can never retroactively re-configure a run that already exists, and the snapshot is taken in the same transaction as the message+run insert. The explain endpoint reflects \"what would a run get *now*\", the snapshot records \"what this run actually got\".\n\n## 4. Tenancy (30 seconds)\n\nSecond registered user requesting your chat's `/effective-config` → **404**, not 403 (no existence leak). The deeper RLS matrix (org-unit ancestor governance etc.) is covered by `configs-rls.integration.spec.ts` in the harness — not worth manual effort.\n\nOne caution: `version` bumping is enforced by the write path in code, and there is no write path yet — so when seeding by hand, bump `version` yourself on UPDATE (as above), otherwise provenance will report a stale version.",
