            "content": "## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Operator config file as instance layer\n\nThe system SHALL load an operator-owned configuration file (`llame.config.json`) at startup and use its contents as the **instance** layer of effective-config resolution. The file SHALL be optional: when absent, the system SHALL boot on documented built-in defaults without error. The file SHALL be treated as deploy-time, version-controllable source of truth (config-as-code), not tenant data.\n\n#### Scenario: File present and valid\n\n- **WHEN** the instance starts with a well-formed `llame.config.json`\n- **THEN** its values populate the instance configuration layer\n- **AND** startup succeeds\n\n#### Scenario: File absent\n\n- **WHEN** the instance starts with no `llame.config.json` present\n- **THEN** the instance configuration layer is the built-in defaults\n- **AND** startup succeeds with no error\n\n#### Scenario: File present but malformed\n\n- **WHEN** the instance starts with a `llame.config.json` that is not valid JSON or violates the config schema\n- **THEN** startup fails loudly with a diagnostic naming the file and the offending path\n- **AND** the instance does not start serving requests on a partial or default config\n\n### Requirement: Environment-variable interpolation in config values\n\nConfig values SHALL support an `{env:NAME}` interpolation token that resolves to the value of the named environment variable at load time. This preserves 12-factor / container-native deployment where configuration is injected via the environment while the file expresses structure.\n\n#### Scenario: Environment variable is set\n\n- **WHEN** a config value contains `{env:DEFAULT_MODEL_ID}` and the environment variable `DEFAULT_MODEL_ID` is set\n- **THEN** the resolved value is the environment variable's contents\n\n#### Scenario: Required environment variable is missing\n\n- **WHEN** a config value contains `{env:NAME}` and `NAME` is unset, with no default provided\n- **THEN** startup fails loudly, naming the config path and the missing variable\n- **AND** the token is never left unresolved in the effective config\n\n#### Scenario: Interpolation with a default\n\n- **WHEN** a config value uses the documented default form (e.g. `{env:NAME:-fallback}`) and `NAME` is unset\n- **THEN** the resolved value is the fallback\n- **AND** startup succeeds\n\n### Requirement: File-path (secret) interpolation in config values\n\nConfig values SHALL support a `{path:LOCATION}` interpolation token that resolves to the trimmed contents of the file at `LOCATION`, supporting Docker/Kubernetes file-mounted secrets so credentials are neither inlined in the config file nor exposed via the process environment.\n\n#### Scenario: Secret file exists\n\n- **WHEN** a config value contains `{path:/run/secrets/openai_key}` and that file exists\n- **THEN** the resolved value is the file's contents (with surrounding whitespace trimmed)\n\n#### Scenario: Required secret file missing\n\n- **WHEN** a config value contains `{path:LOCATION}` and no file exists at `LOCATION`\n- **THEN** startup fails loudly, naming the config path and the missing file location\n- **AND** the token is never left unresolved\n\n#### Scenario: Resolved secret values are not logged\n\n- **WHEN** any `{path:…}` or `{env:…}` value resolves to a credential\n- **THEN** the resolved value is never written to logs, error messages, or the explain endpoint output\n\n### Requirement: Instance config precedence over ambient environment\n\nWhere the same instance setting can be expressed both in `llame.config.json` and as a legacy environment variable, the file value SHALL take precedence, and the environment variable SHALL be honored only as a fallback when the file does not set that key. This SHALL be applied consistently so an operator can migrate a setting from env to file without changing its effect.\n\n#### Scenario: File overrides a legacy env var\n\n- **WHEN** both `llame.config.json` sets `compaction.tokenThreshold` and the legacy `COMPACTION_TOKEN_THRESHOLD` env var is set\n- **THEN** the file value is used\n- **AND** the resolved instance layer records the file as the source\n\n#### Scenario: Env var used as fallback\n\n- **WHEN** `llame.config.json` does not set a key but its legacy env var is set\n- **THEN** the env var value populates that instance-layer key\n",
