            "content": "## 1. Instance config file + interpolation (`instance-config`)\n\n- [ ] 1.1 Define the typed instance-config schema (live keys `run.maxOutputTokens`, `compaction.tokenThreshold`; reserve top-level namespaces by convention) with strict validation (unknown key / type violation → named error).\n- [ ] 1.2 Implement the `llame.config.json` loader: locate (documented path + optional override), parse, validate; absent file → built-in defaults, malformed → loud startup failure naming the offending path.\n- [ ] 1.3 Implement one-pass, non-recursive value interpolation: `{env:NAME}`, `{env:NAME:-default}`, `{path:LOCATION}` (trimmed file contents); required-but-unresolved token → loud startup failure naming config path + missing source.\n- [ ] 1.4 Guarantee resolved secret values are never logged, never surfaced in errors, and never included in explain output (redaction at the boundary).\n- [ ] 1.5 Wire file → env precedence: file value wins; legacy instance env vars (`COMPACTION_TOKEN_THRESHOLD`, `RUN_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`, model-default) honored only as fallback; provenance records which source won.\n- [ ] 1.6 Unit tests for every `instance-config` spec scenario (present/absent/malformed, env set/missing/default, path present/missing, no-secret-logging, file-vs-env precedence).\n\n## 2. Tenant config-scope store (`effective-config` storage)\n\n- [ ] 2.1 `configs` table: `(scope_type ∈ {org_unit,user,chat}, scope_id)` unique, `config jsonb`, `version` bumped per write, timestamps. Generate migration (renumbered after current master head; never hand-edit numbers/prevId).\n- [ ] 2.2 RLS `ENABLE` + `FORCE` with read/write policies: own user scope; owned-chat scope; org-unit scope gated via memberships including ancestor-governance (a config bound at an org root binds child-team members). Append `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` by hand to the generated SQL; `drizzle-kit check`.\n- [ ] 2.3 Repository: `findByScopes` filters by `(scope_type, scope_id)` in-database (composite index, no cross-type scan); single-document-per-scope read.\n- [ ] 2.4 RLS integration tests: enabled+forced; cross-tenant user read/write denied; chat-scope non-owner denied; org-unit stranger denied + member-can't-write; **ancestor-governance regression** (child-unit member reads parent-scoped config, stranger sees nothing, child member can't write); absent-identity fails closed.\n\n## 3. Resolution engine (`effective-config` core)\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Layer model: instance (from §1) → org-unit → user → chat; skip non-applicable layers without affecting outcome.\n- [ ] 3.2 Deterministic merge: objects deep-merge, arrays replace wholesale (incl. empty-array-replaces); later wins. Unit tests for the merge scenarios.\n- [ ] 3.3 Per-leaf provenance (scope + version) and consulted-layer chain (includes layers that set nothing); drop stale provenance when a subtree replaces a scalar at the same path.\n- [ ] 3.4 Export typed accessors for downstream consumers (`snapshotMaxOutputTokens`, `snapshotCompactionThreshold`) reading from a snapshot — even though nothing consumes them in this slice (stable seam).\n\n## 4. Per-run snapshot (`effective-config` durability)\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Add immutable `runs.config_snapshot` (migration alongside §2.1).\n- [ ] 4.2 Resolve effective config once at run creation and freeze onto the run **inside the same transaction** that persists the triggering message + run (`persistUserMessageAndRun`).\n- [ ] 4.3 Execution reads configuration only from the snapshot — audit that no execution path re-resolves live.\n- [ ] 4.4 Tests: snapshot frozen at creation; mid-flight config edit does not retroactively apply (two-run divergence); message+run+snapshot persist atomically (failure → no partial state).\n\n## 5. Explain endpoint (`effective-config` audit surface)\n\n- [ ] 5.1 `GET /api/v1/chats/:id/effective-config` (auth-required) → effective config + per-leaf provenance + consulted layers via live resolution within the caller's tenant transaction.\n- [ ] 5.2 Fail-closed: cross-tenant / unknown id → `404` (no existence leak); unauthenticated → `401`. Regenerate `openapi.json` via build (never hand-merge).\n- [ ] 5.3 e2e tests: owner explains; cross-tenant 404 indistinguishable from not-found; unauth 401; explain diverges from an older run's snapshot after an edit.\n\n## 6. Docs, config surface, and cleanup\n\n- [ ] 6.1 Add a documented `llame.config.json` example; update `.env.example` and deployment docs to frame instance env vars as fallbacks/interpolation targets, not the primary path.\n- [ ] 6.2 Amend SPEC §6.3–§6.4 (operator-file instance layer + interpolation + snapshot) and add a VISION \"emerging directions\" note on the operator-code / tenant-data config boundary.\n- [ ] 6.3 Fold away the superseded `org_units.settings` blob (no consumer) in favor of the uniform mechanism; note the migration.\n- [ ] 6.4 Update `apps/api/AGENTS.md` hand-authored-migration gotcha list and module-boundary description.\n\n## 7. Verification\n\n- [ ] 7.1 `pnpm --filter api build` (regenerates openapi.json), `--filter api typecheck`, `--filter api lint` clean.\n- [ ] 7.2 `pnpm --filter api test` green (unit + integration, DB-gated where applicable).\n- [ ] 7.3 `bash apps/api/scripts/rls-test.sh` green: instance-config, resolver, snapshot, and configs-RLS suites (incl. ancestor-governance).\n- [ ] 7.4 `openspec validate layered-effective-config` clean; every spec scenario maps to at least one executed test.\n",
