            "content": "## 1. Config schema + loader\n\n- [ ] 1.1 Define the strict, closed, typed schema for `llame.config.json` covering the currently-migrated instance settings (model default id, title-generation model id, and instance-level scalar defaults). Unknown key / wrong type → validation error naming the path.\n- [ ] 1.2 Implement the loader: resolve the config path (documented default + `LLAME_CONFIG_PATH`-style override), read + parse; absent file → built-in defaults, malformed/schema-violating → loud boot failure naming the offending path.\n- [ ] 1.3 Wire the loader into startup ahead of the current `ConfigService` reads for the migrated keys, so a failed load aborts boot before serving requests.\n\n## 2. Value interpolation\n\n- [ ] 2.1 Implement single-pass, non-recursive interpolation for `{env:NAME}` and `{env:NAME:-default}`; required-but-unresolved → loud boot failure naming config path + variable.\n- [ ] 2.2 Implement `{path:LOCATION}` interpolation (trimmed file contents) for file-mounted secrets; missing required file → loud boot failure naming config path + location.\n- [ ] 2.3 Redact at the boundary: resolved interpolation values never enter logs, errors, or diagnostics — errors reference the source (variable/path), never the value.\n\n## 3. Precedence + migrated settings\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Implement file → env → built-in-default precedence, applied consistently per setting; record/return which source supplied each value (for future provenance, and for tests).\n- [ ] 3.2 Migrate the current instance env vars into the schema/file as first inhabitants; keep their env vars working as documented fallbacks/interpolation targets (no behavior change for existing deploys).\n\n## 4. Tests\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Loader: file present/valid, absent→defaults, malformed→boot fail, unknown-key→boot fail, wrong-type→boot fail.\n- [ ] 4.2 Interpolation: env set / missing-required-fail / with-default; path present / missing-required-fail; no-secret-in-logs (negative asserti