D}\n# tokens (the committed example does, with sensible :- defaults).\nDEFAULT_MODEL_ID=system:openai:gpt-5.4-mini\nTITLE_GENERATION_MODEL_ID=system:openai:gpt-5.4-nano\n\n# Context window of the configured model, in tokens (e.g. 128000, 1000000). Used to\n# derive the conversation-compaction trigger (#57): compact at 80% of the window.\n# Known models (src/models/model-catalog.ts) are derived automatically — set this only\n# to override, or when running a model the catalog doesn't know (arbitrary\n# OPENAI_BASE_URL endpoints). Empty + unknown model = conservative default (100000).\nMODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS=\n\n# Explicit compaction trigger override, in tokens (#57): when the chat's live context\n# (real usage of the last turn, estimated as a fallback) exceeds this, older turns are\n# summarized into a lineage row and only the summary + recent turns are sent to the\n# model. Takes precedence over the MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS derivation. Usually\n# leave empty; the eval suite sets it very low to exercise compaction cheaply.\nCOMPACTION_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=\n\n# Run liveness (#48). A per-run deadman job fires runs.timeoutSeconds\n# (default 300) after enqueue: a terminal run is left alone, a run with a fresh\n# heartbeat is re-checked later, and a run whose heartbeat is older than\n# runs.heartbeatStaleSeconds (default 60) is expired. The executing worker\n# stamps the heartbeat every runs.heartbeatSeconds (default 15).\n# Configure in llame.config.json (runs.*); these variables are interpolation\n# targets only, usable via {env:...} tokens in the file.\nRUN_HEARTBEAT_SECONDS=\nRUN_HEARTBEAT_STALE_SECONDS=\nRUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=\n\n# Behind a reverse proxy, set http.trustProxy in llame.config.json to the hop\n# count (e.g. 1) or an Express subnet spec so session.ip records the real\n# client, not the proxy (#68). Leave unset when clients connect directly —\n# trusting proxy headers with no proxy lets clients spoof their IP. This\n# variable is an interpolation target