nt, test updates).\n\nNo `APPROVED` or `CHANGES_REQUESTED` reviews present — both are `COMMENTED` only.\n\n---\n\n### Inline review threads — filtered to UNRESOLVED (3 of 3 total; none resolved)\n\n#### 1. gemini-code-assist\n**File:** `apps/web/app/(admin)/admin/organizations/components/org-tree.tsx:147`\n**Thread ID:** `PRRT********JjUe` · **Comment ID:** `PRRC********gCGz` (databaseId `3565167027`)\n**Resolved:** false · **Outdated:** false\n\n&gt; [medium] In WAI-ARIA tree views, only one tree item should be focusable via Tab (using `tabIndex={0}`), while all other items should have `tabIndex={-1}`. Having `tabIndex={0}` on every row forces keyboard users to tab through every single organization unit in the tree, which can be extremely tedious and violates standard accessibility patterns. Consider passing `tabIndex` as a prop from the parent `OrgUnitsTree` component where `selectedId` is managed, so that only the selected row (or the first row if none is selected) is focusable.\n\n#### 2. gemini-code-assist\n**File:** `apps/web/app/(admin)/admin/organizations/components/org-tree.tsx:442`\n**Thread ID:** `PRRT********JjUg` · **Comment ID:** `PRRC********gCG1` (databaseId `3565167029`)\n**Resolved:** false · **Outdated:** false\n\n&gt; [medium] Browsers typically disable all pointer and mouse events on disabled form controls (like `&lt;button disabled&gt;`), which prevents the native `title` tooltip from being displayed on hover. To ensure the explanation for why the button is disabled is actually readable by users, wrap the disabled button in a `span` element that carries the `title` attribute.\n&gt;\n&gt; ```jsx\n&gt; &lt;span\n&gt;   title=\"Members panel is the next step — deferred to the fast-follow change (D7).\"\n&gt;   className=\"ml-auto shrink-0 opacity-55\"\n&gt; &gt;\n&gt;   &lt;Button variant=\"outline\" size=\"sm\" disabled className=\"pointer-events-none\"&gt;\n&gt;     &lt;UsersIcon /&gt;\n&gt;     Manage members\n&gt;   &lt;/Button&gt;\n&gt; &lt;/