que-and-real findings over the last N PRs, drop them. Worth a 10-minute audit over PRs #170–176 before the next one.\n\n## 7. Design QA loop — three screenshot rounds that were predictable\n\nThe Card `gap-6` spacing drift, footer background, and title alignment each took a human-eyeball round. The lesson is already codified (mock inline CSS is the spec; extract a metric table upfront), but the *process* still relies on you catching it. Options: (a) enforce the metric-table step in the design brief before any implementation agent starts — zero infra, already your convention, just make it a gate; (b) Playwright screenshot comparison against the mock — I'd hold off; the mocks aren't pixel-stable enough yet and the maintenance cost of visual snapshots is real. (a) only.\n\n## 8. Paper cuts worth batching into one cleanup PR\n\n- **lefthook #173** (`LEFTHOOK=0` for deletions) — fix the hook, delete the folklore.\n- **`pnpm --filter api test -- --maxWorkers=2` arg-swallowing** — add a `test:fast` script so nobody hits the jest-pattern trap again.\n- **Committed `openapi.json`** — it conflicted on the ripple merge and will again. Either generate it in CI and diff-check (fail if stale) or accept the conflicts; right now you have the worst of both (committed *and* manually regenerated).\n- **Subagents don't inherit MCP/design tools** — the \"extract design file to temp first\" step worked; make it a standing convention in the orchestration prompt template rather than a per-session discovery.\n- **Next.js 16 one-dev-per-project-dir** — already mitigated via the `llame-dev` worktree; just make sure that's in AGENTS.md so agents don't rediscover it (currently only in my memory).\n\n## Prioritized plan (leverage order)\n\n1. **rtk: fail-loud/passthrough semantics** — it taxes literally every session and corrupts trust in negative results. Yours to fix, small diff.\n2. **`db:rebase` script** — converts the migration ritual (your named pain) into one command; also neutralizes the