            "content": "## Goal\n\nTurn chat search from the shipped ILIKE MVP (#143) into **hybrid, multilingual, Postgres-native retrieval** — and then into the assistant's **episodic memory**. The `search_conversations` tool already rides the exact same repository method as the web palette (`ChatsRepository.searchByOwner`, tool-loop D7 \"one search path\"), so every retrieval-quality upgrade below automatically upgrades the agent's recall of past conversations. That end state — a self-hosted assistant whose recall over its own verbatim history is hybrid, multilingual, provider-optional, and RLS-isolated — is the differentiator; plain \"better search\" is just the substrate.\n\nGrounding: internal memory research (2026-07) concluded **verbatim retrieval > fact extraction** for this class of memory. The search projection *is* the episodic store; there is no extraction pipeline in this plan. SPEC §20 curated/semantic memory stays a **separate, later** concern — this umbrella deliberately does not grow into it.\n\n## Architecture (agreed)\n\nDerived **search projection** inside Postgres — canonical `chats`/`messages` stay untouched:\n\n- `search_documents`: overlapping contextual chunks (several adjacent messages, ~300–800 tokens, message-boundary splits, role markers, versioned chunker, content-hashed). Serializes **text parts of user/assistant turns only** — same exclusion policy as today's search (never system prompts or tool internals).\n- Three independent retrievers over those documents: `simple`-config FTS (generated tsvector, GIN), trigram via **`word_similarity`** (GIN `gin_trgm_ops`; plain `similarity()` between a short query and an 800-token chunk is near-zero by construction — the query-in-document operators are the correct tool), and pgvector cosine (exact scan first, HNSW only after measurement).\n- **Reciprocal Rank Fusion** of ranks (never raw-score mixing), then weighted top-3 document aggregation per chat.\n- Provider-neutral `EmbeddingBackend` interface + versioned embedding-model registry (`model_key`, dimensions, doc/query prefixes); dimensionless `vector` column so model generations coexist; content-hash guard so a delayed batch result can never overwrite newer content.\n- Async indexing on **pg-boss** (the existing queue substrate — no bespoke `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` dirty-table; per-chat `singletonKey` gives the same coalescing).\n- No language detection anywhere. `simple` FTS + trigrams + multilingual embeddings cover ru/en/es and mixed-language chats; language-specific tokenization (PGroonga etc.) only if the eval set proves a gap.\n\n## Non-negotiable invariants\n\n- **RLS is the guard, not the app filter.** `search_documents` / `search_embeddings` get `ENABLE` + `FORCE` RLS (owner policies over denormalized `owner_user_id`); every candidate query runs under `runAs`. The explicit owner filter inside candidate CTEs stays as the seatbelt. **No public-read policy on search tables** — a `visibility = 'public'` chat is readable via `runAsPublic`, but must never surface in anyone else's search or be reachable through the search path. Negative tests ship with every phase (cross-tenant + public-chat exclusion), wired into `scripts/rls-test.sh`.\n- **Freshness is split per retriever.** Lexical projection rebuild: seconds–minutes after a message lands (no regression vs. today's live ILIKE). Embeddings: lazy/batched, up to 24 h acceptable.\n- Derived index is rebuildable from the canonical tables at any time (SPEC §2.1); embeddings are artifacts tied to an exact model revision — model migration is register → backfill → evaluate → activate → retire, never overwrite in place.\n- No secrets or provider config ever enter document text.\n\n## Phases (sub-issues)\n\n1. **Search platform without embeddings** — projection + chunker + FTS + `word_similarity` trigrams + pg-boss reindexing + relevance eval set. Fixes #171 on the web side. No new infra (pg_trgm is contrib).\n2. **Chat embedding layer, no search** — model registry, `search_embeddings`, one `EmbeddingBackend` + batch pipeline, backfill. Query path untouched while the async machinery bakes.\n3. **Hybrid retrieval** — synchronous query embedding + 3-leg RRF + chat aggregation, tuned against the phase-1 eval baseline.\n4. **Episodic memory semantics** — temporal filters/provenance on `search_conversations`, recency as ranking-only signal, recall-time injection framing.\n\nSequencing is strict 1 → 2 → 3; 4 can start once 1 exists (it improves further as 2–3 land).\n\n## Decisions still open (gate phase 2, not phase 1)\n\n- [ ] **pgvector deployment requirement**: swap `postgres:17-alpine` → a pgvector-enabled image (e.g. `pgvector/pgvector:pg17`) in `compose.yaml`, `scripts/rls-test.sh`, CI; document as a self-host requirement.\n- [ ] **Whose credentials embed the chats (BYOK tension)**: proposed — embedding model is **operator config** (`llame.config.json`, like model defaults; background indexing is instance-scoped, not per-request BYOK), with a local/Ollama backend (bge-m3-class multilingual) as the flagship self-hosted answer. No config ⇒ no embeddings ⇒ search stays lexical (fail closed, feature-degrade not error).\n- [ ] Index compaction summaries (`compactions.summary`) as search documents — high-signal, proposed for a later pass, not v1.\n- [ ] Forked chats duplicate content across lineage — accept duplicate hits in v1; revisit if noisy.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\n- SPEC §20 curated/semantic memory (separate store, separate write policy).\n- Knowledge Spaces / RAG over external sources (`knowledge` roadmap) — same retrieval machinery may be reused later, but this umbrella indexes chat history only.\n- Auto-recall injection into new runs (phase 4 is tool-first; auto-recall is a possible follow-up with its own safety review).\n- HNSW, PGroonga, dedicated queue — each only after measurements demand it.\n\nRefs #143 (shipped MVP + its named FTS/pg_trgm follow-up), #171, #57, memory-research conclusions (2026-07).