            "content": "Phase 1 of the chat-search → episodic-memory umbrella. Replaces the ILIKE MVP's retrieval (#143's named follow-up) with an indexed, ranked, typo-tolerant lexical search — and builds the projection platform phases 2–4 stand on. **No embeddings, no new infra**: `pg_trgm` ships in Postgres contrib; the projection here is deliberately embedding-ready so phase 2 adds columns/tables, not rebuilds.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Search projection**\n- `search_documents` table: `owner_user_id` (denormalized, text — matches `users.id`), `chat_id` FK cascade, `chunk_ordinal`, `chunker_version`, first/last message id + timestamps, `content`, `normalized_content`, `content_hash`, generated `fts tsvector` (`simple` config) STORED, `UNIQUE (chat_id, chunk_ordinal, chunker_version)`.\n- **RLS `ENABLE` + `FORCE`**, owner policy on `owner_user_id = current_setting('app.current_user_id', true)`. No public-read policy — public chats are excluded from the search path entirely.\n- Deterministic chunker: message-boundary chunks of several adjacent user/assistant turns (~300–800 tokens via a character cap — tokenizer-independent), 1–2 message overlap, `[user]`/`[assistant]` role markers, **text parts only** (same exclusion policy as `searchByOwner` today: never system/tool content). Normalization: NFKC, newline/whitespace collapse, lowercase; keep accents, code, identifiers, URLs. Versioned (`chunker_version`); content-hash per chunk.\n- Indexes: GIN on `fts`, GIN `gin_trgm_ops` on `normalized_content`, `(owner_user_id, chat_id)`, `(owner_user_id, last_message_at DESC)`.\n\n**Async projection maintenance (pg-boss)**\n- On message insert (and delete/chat-delete), enqueue a per-chat reindex job in the same transaction pattern the run pipeline uses; `singletonKey = chat_id` for coalescing. Full-rebuild-per-dirty-chat; content hashes make unchanged chunks no-ops. Freshness target: **seconds–minutes** (lexical search must not regress vs. today's live ILIKE).\n- Backfill job for existing chats.\n- Chat deletion cascades; message edits/deletes rebuild overlapping chunks (rebuild-all-per-chat covers this in v1).\n\n**Query path**\n- Rewrite `ChatsRepository.searchByOwner` (same signature/callers — web palette + `search_conversations` tool keep working unchanged) to: FTS candidates (`websearch_to_tsquery('simple', …)`, `ts_rank_cd`) + trigram candidates via **`word_similarity`** (`<%` operators — NOT `similarity()`, which is length-crushed for query-vs-chunk), RRF-fused at document level, weighted top-3 aggregation per chat, snippet from the best document (`ts_headline` for lexical matches).\n- Keep the explicit owner filter inside every candidate CTE as the seatbelt; RLS is the guard.\n\n**Web (fixes #171)**\n- Command palette stops re-filtering server search results through cmdk's client-side filter — server rank order is authoritative. Case-insensitivity asserted end-to-end on both match paths incl. non-ASCII casing (Cyrillic), per #171's acceptance criteria.\n\n**Relevance eval set (consumed by phase 3)**\n- Small versioned dataset in-repo: exact phrases, names/identifiers, error messages, paraphrases, ru/en/es queries, **inflected-Russian forms** (the known `simple`-config weakness — measure it now so phase 3 can prove the embedding lift), mixed-language, typos, transliterations, code/filenames. Track Recall@10, MRR, zero-result rate, p50/p95 latency.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Cross-tenant negative test: another owner's exactly-matching content never surfaces (both directions) — in `rls-test.sh`.\n- [ ] Public-chat negative test: a `visibility='public'` chat of another user never surfaces in search.\n- [ ] System/tool message content is neither indexed nor matched nor snippeted.\n- [ ] Exact-title-lowercased and content-term-uppercased queries return the chat (both surfaces, #171).\n- [ ] Typo'd and partial-word queries return the chat (trigram leg).\n- [ ] New message searchable within the freshness target without manual action.\n- [ ] Projection fully rebuildable from `messages` via the backfill job.\n- [ ] Eval baseline recorded.\n\nOut of scope: embeddings (phase 2), compaction-summary indexing, HNSW, language-specific tokenizers.\n\nFixes #171. Refs #143.\n",
