            "content": "## What\n\nCommits the chat-search research pair under `docs/research/chat-search/`, structured after the existing `docs/research/long-term-memory/` track (dated source import + synthesized cross-report):\n\n- `2026-07-11-postgresql-multilingual-chat-search-chatgpt-com.md` — the external (chatgpt.com deep-research) PostgreSQL-native multilingual chat-search architecture recommendation, imported **verbatim** (its author had no knowledge of this codebase).\n- `2026-07-12-chat-search-cross-report.md` — the reviewed/adopted artifact: codebase grounding (shipped tool loop + `search_conversations` sharing `searchByOwner`, RLS FORCE tenancy, pg-boss substrate, `postgres:17-alpine` extension availability), the corrections (`word_similarity` over `similarity()`, RLS-as-guard inversion, pg-boss over a bespoke dirty-chat queue, per-retriever freshness split, Drizzle-convention fit, operator-config embedding resolution for the BYOK tension), adopted judgments, and the refined 4-phase plan.\n\n## Relationship to other tracks\n\n- The `long-term-memory` research (separate branch) covers **factual/semantic** memory (SPEC §20 curated store). This track covers **episodic** memory — recall over verbatim chat history — building on that track's verbatim-over-extraction verdict. Deliberately separate stores.\n- Plan of record: tracker #194 with sub-issues #195–#198; the issues reference these docs as their design rationale.\n\nDocs-only change: no code, no migrations, not format-gated (CI's `format:check` is scoped to `apps/api`). The cross-report is prettier-formatted; the import is kept byte-verbatim.\n\nRefs #194.\n",
