            "content": "## Chat search → episodic memory: hybrid Postgres-native retrieval as the assistant's recall\n\nTurn chat search from the shipped ILIKE MVP (#143) into hybrid, multilingual, Postgres-native retrieval — and then into the assistant's **episodic memory**. The smallest useful version is phase 1 alone (indexed, ranked, typo-tolerant lexical search that also upgrades the `search_conversations` tool, since it shares `ChatsRepository.searchByOwner` with the web palette — tool-loop D7). Explicitly deferred: SPEC §20 curated/semantic memory (separate store, the factual-memory research track), Knowledge Spaces / external-source RAG (v0.6, #39), auto-recall injection into runs without a tool call, and every scale upgrade (HNSW, PGroonga, dedicated queue) until measurements demand it.\n\n### Architecture overview\n\nA derived **search projection** over the canonical `chats`/`messages` (which stay untouched): contextual multi-message chunks in `search_documents` (#195), three independent retrievers — `simple`-config FTS, `word_similarity` trigrams, pgvector cosine (#196) — fused by Reciprocal Rank Fusion at query time (#197), with episodic semantics (temporal filters, provenance, recency-as-ranking, safe recall framing) layered on the tool surface (#198). Async indexing rides pg-boss (SPEC §9; the existing run-queue substrate), embeddings sit behind a provider-neutral backend + versioned model registry. Full design rationale, source research, and the corrections we made to it: [`docs/research/chat-search/`](https://github.com/leon0399/llame/tree/worktree-docs-chat-search-research/docs/research/chat-search) — source import + cross-report (lands via #199).\n\n### Key design decisions\n\n- **Verbatim retrieval over fact extraction** — the projection IS the episodic store; no extraction pipeline (2026-07 memory-landscape research verdict; cross-report §1).\n- **RLS is the guard, the owner filter is the seatbelt** — `search_documents`/`search_embeddings` get `ENABLE`+`FORCE` owner policies over denormalized `owner_user_id`; **no public-read policy on search tables** (a public chat must never surface in anyone else's search). Cross-tenant + public-chat negative tests ship with every phase, wired into `scripts/rls-test.sh`.\n- **`word_similarity()`, not `similarity()`, for the trigram leg** — plain `similarity()` is length-crushed for a short query vs. an 800-token chunk and would contribute nothing to fusion (cross-report §3.1).\n- **pg-boss with per-chat `singletonKey`, not a bespoke dirty-chat queue** — one job substrate; content-hash idempotency makes reindexing coalescing-safe (cross-report §3.3).\n- **Freshness split per retriever** — lexical projection rebuilds in seconds–minutes (no regression vs. today's live ILIKE); embeddings lazy/batched up to 24 h (cross-report §3.4).\n- **RRF over ranks, never raw-score mixing**; weighted top-3 document aggregation per chat; all constants tuned against the phase-1 eval set, not intuition.\n- **Embedding model is operator config** (`llame.config.json`), resolving the BYOK tension for instance-scoped background indexing; local/Ollama backend is the flagship self-hosted answer; absent config ⇒ lexical-only, fail-closed feature degrade (cross-report §3.6).\n- **No language detection anywhere** — `simple` FTS + trigrams + multilingual embeddings cover ru/en/es and mixed-language chats; the eval set measures the known inflected-Russian lexical weakness so phase 3 can prove the embedding lift.\n- **Exact vector scan first; HNSW only after a measured p95 breach** (per-model partial cast index over the dimensionless `vector` column).\n\n## Tracks\n\n### 🔎 Retrieval — projection, embeddings, hybrid fusion\n\n- [ ] #195 — search platform: chat projection + FTS + trigram (no embeddings) _(fixes #171; no new infra — pg_trgm is contrib)_\n- [ ] #196 — chat embedding layer: registry, pgvector storage, backends, backfill (no search) _(requires #195; gated on pgvector image + operator-config decision below)_\n- [ ] #197 — hybrid retrieval: query embeddings + RRF fusion + scoring _(requires #196 and the #195 eval baseline)_\n\n### 🧠 Memory — episodic semantics on the tool surface\n\n- [ ] #198 — episodic memory: temporal recall, provenance, recency ranking, safe recall framing _(requires #195; full value after #197)_\n\n### Track & dependency graph\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph retrieval[\"🔎 Retrieval\"]\n        P1[\"#195 projection + FTS/trgm\"]\n        P2[\"#196 embedding layer\"]\n        P3[\"#197 hybrid RRF\"]\n        P1 --> P2 --> P3\n    end\n\n    subgraph memory[\"🧠 Memory\"]\n        P4[\"#198 episodic semantics\"]\n    end\n\n    %% cross-track edges (blocker --> blocked)\n    P1 --> P4\n    P3 -. quality compounds .-> P4\n\n    classDef todo fill:#fff6d6,stroke:#caa106,color:#3a2f04;\n    class P1,P2,P3,P4 todo;\n```\n\n### Build order\n\n1. **#195** — no blockers; also produces the relevance eval baseline everything downstream is judged against.\n2. **Gates for #196 (decide during #195):** pgvector-enabled image (e.g. `pgvector/pgvector:pg17`) across `compose.yaml` / `scripts/rls-test.sh` / CI, documented as a self-host requirement; operator-config embedding backend in `llame.config.json`.\n3. **#196**, then **#197** (eval-gated: RRF must beat each individual retriever or stop and re-tune).\n4. **#198** — may start any time after #195 (temporal/provenance/framing are retrieval-agnostic); recall quality compounds as #196–#197 land.\n\n### Success criteria\n\n- Cross-tenant and public-chat negative tests green in `rls-test.sh` for every search table and every retrieval leg.\n- Exact-title-lowercased, typo'd, paraphrased, and cross-language (ru/en/es) eval queries return the right chat; eval deltas recorded per phase (Recall@10, MRR, zero-result rate, p50/p95).\n- New message lexically searchable within seconds–minutes with no manual action; embeddings within 24 h; an instance with no embedding config runs clean on lexical-only.\n- `search_conversations` answers \"when did we discuss X\" with chat/date/message-range provenance, recency never suppresses a strong old match, and recalled excerpts are framed as data, not instructions.\n- Projection + embeddings fully rebuildable from canonical tables; model migration (register → backfill → evaluate → activate → retire) demonstrated without data loss.\n\n### Open decisions (owned here)\n\n- [ ] pgvector image swap + self-host requirement docs _(gates #196)_\n- [ ] Operator-config embedding backend (proposed: `llame.config.json`, Ollama-first) _(gates #196)_\n- [ ] Index `compactions.summary` as search documents _(deferred past v1)_\n- [ ] Fork-lineage duplicate hits _(accepted in v1; revisit if noisy)_\n\nRefs #143 (shipped MVP), #171, #57, #39 (v0.6 Knowledge epic — the retrieval machinery here is a deliberate precursor, but this tracker indexes chat history only), #199 (research docs).\n",
